    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by similar works in loop scenarios </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This time, you're trapped in a <strong>Japanese convenience store</strong>, and it\u00b4s <strong>nighttime</strong>! The difficulty has been raised\u2014find every <strong>anomaly</strong> and <strong>escape through the correct door</strong>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game relies on detailed visual observation, so unfamiliar language <strong>won</strong>\u00b4<strong>t</strong> hinder your experience. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are <strong>dozens of anomalies</strong>, along with <strong>a few jump scares</strong>, creating a <strong>slightly</strong> eerie atmosphere. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But don\u00b4t worry about the abundance of items in the convenience store. We have balanced the game\u00b4s difficulty to some extent\u2014this is not an extremely hardcore spot-the-difference game. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You also don\u00b4t need to worry too much about the jump scare elements. This isn\u00b4t a game focused on heavy horror. The few mild jump scares are mainly added to enhance the fun.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The only advice is to keep a strong impression of <strong>Scene Zero</strong>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To maintain a consistent difficulty level, we\u2019ve disabled adjustments to brightness, FOV, and other visual settings in the game. Only basic settings like resolution and fullscreen/windowed modes are available. While you can adjust your monitor settings, it\u2019s highly discouraged as it may impact the intended game experience. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Playtime: </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game duration heavily depends on your observational skills\u2014you might finish in just <i>a few minutes</i>, or perhaps <i>never</i> escape...</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by similar works in loop scenarios </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This time, you're trapped in a <strong>Japanese convenience store</strong>, and it\u00b4s <strong>nighttime</strong>! The difficulty has been raised\u2014find every <strong>anomaly</strong> and <strong>escape through the correct door</strong>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game relies on detailed visual observation, so unfamiliar language <strong>won</strong>\u00b4<strong>t</strong> hinder your experience. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are <strong>dozens of anomalies</strong>, along with <strong>a few jump scares</strong>, creating a <strong>slightly</strong> eerie atmosphere. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But don\u00b4t worry about the abundance of items in the convenience store. We have balanced the game\u00b4s difficulty to some extent\u2014this is not an extremely hardcore spot-the-difference game. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You also don\u00b4t need to worry too much about the jump scare elements. This isn\u00b4t a game focused on heavy horror. The few mild jump scares are mainly added to enhance the fun.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The only advice is to keep a strong impression of <strong>Scene Zero</strong>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To maintain a consistent difficulty level, we\u2019ve disabled adjustments to brightness, FOV, and other visual settings in the game. Only basic settings like resolution and fullscreen/windowed modes are available. While you can adjust your monitor settings, it\u2019s highly discouraged as it may impact the intended game experience. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Playtime: </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game duration heavily depends on your observational skills\u2014you might finish in just <i>a few minutes</i>, or perhaps <i>never</i> escape...</p>",
